      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right that it's all net neutral from a purely logical standpoint—there's no cosmic scoreboard. But \"better\" isn't about the outcome; it's about the experience itself. Staying means you get to feel the sun on your face, taste good food, or laugh at a dumb joke—even if those moments are fleeting. Leaving closes the door on all possible future moments, good or bad. So it's not that staying is objectively better—it's that you might as well stick around to see what happens next.",
